fails: A bigger firm brings out something like it first, and the savings are gone.

# ================================================================ a new job at last

== bold: a new job at last / G
base: go back to the line of work you know, close to home, for good
likelier_if: has [old family name] +10; has [contact in the trade] +5
- G | turn down the city money for the old yard where your family worked | v: tradition, security | act: turn down the city money and take the post at the old yard where their family worked | chance: 45 | grants: crew that has your back | takes_if_fails: family who will always take you in
works: The old hands at the yard take {N} in as one of their own, and stand by {N} from the first week.
works: Within a month the crew knows {Ns} name and {Ns} family's, and they cover for each other without being asked.
fails: The yard lays off its newest hands before the spring. {N} blames {parent} for the city money turned down, and the two stop speaking.
fails: The old yard is closing, it turns out, and the quarrel with {parent} over it shuts the family door on {N}.

